{
  "about": "`webagents cron list` and `webagents cron run <agent> <name>` (plan item 1.7, 2026-09-26): the same help and the same lines in both CLIs. The help words are compared by tests/cli/test_cli_parity.py (TypeScript src/cli/index.ts is the reference; `help` here is what both declare). The lines are rendered by Python cli/cron_command.py (render_schedule_table, run_line) and TypeScript src/cli/cron-action.ts (renderScheduleTable, runLine), run by tests/cli/test_cron_cli_w1daemon.py and tests/unit/cli/cron-w1daemon.test.ts. `list` reads the folder's agent files as the daemon would and the runner's state under each agent's .webagents/cron/, writing nothing; `run` builds the one agent the way the daemon does, runs the schedule now as the owner, delivers as configured and records the run in that state.",
